      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "We had a need to add a callback sink to our logs so we can reprocess log messages to different formats (json and MQTT) while keeping the original logging. I discovered a small trap based on not knowing the C++ standard inside out. To add a sink, be careful how you access ",
          "position": {
            "start": {
              "line": 3,
              "column": 1,
              "offset": 69
            },
            "end": {
              "line": 3,
              "column": 273,
              "offset": 341
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "inlineCode",
          "value": "sinks()",
          "position": {
            "start": {
              "line": 3,
              "column": 273,
              "offset": 341
            },
            "end": {
              "line": 3,
              "column": 282,
              "offset": 350
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": " in the logger. This doesn't work:",
          "position": {
            "start": {
              "line": 3,
              "column": 282,
              "offset": 350
            },
            "end": {
              "line": 3,
              "column": 316,
              "offset": 384
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "position": {
        "start": {
          "line": 3,
